{"Comment claims Django ORM handles negative slicing automatically but Django QuerySets do NOT support negative indexing for SQL-backed queries - will raise AssertionError": 0.9468435645103455, "organization_context.member.has_global_access may fail for contexts where the user isn't represented as a member": 0.3237447440624237, "Using a query parameter as a feature toggle bypasses Sentry's feature flag infrastructure - no centralized rollout control or kill-switch capability": 0.5973202586174011, "Using a query parameter as a feature toggle creates inconsistent API contract - same endpoint behaves differently based on ad-hoc parameter": 0.4768308997154236, "Using a query parameter as a feature toggle provides limited observability for tracking adoption/issues": 0.09106668084859848, "Using a query parameter as a feature toggle enables users to self-select into experimental code paths": 0.37594595551490784, "Authorization check conflates authorization (who can access data) with feature rollout (who gets new code paths), preventing staged rollout to specific test organizations": 0.09311641752719879, "No explicit guardrails on magnitude of negative offsets - malicious cursor could specify extremely large negative offsets causing pathological query behavior or resource exhaustion": 0.8174940347671509, "OptimizedCursorPaginator duplicates ~90 lines of logic from existing paginator implementations rather than using composition or subclassing, creating maintenance burden": 0.621135413646698}